 **Assignment resolution (Founder clarification).** Explicit host instructions in the issue description, or Founder comments directly assigning that issue to phoebe-dev, are valid independently of the target registry. Discover through complete board pagination, issue descriptions and recent Founder comments. The independent eligible-work.py inventory is fail-closed; unreachable board records are errors, not an empty queue. SoringP1 #301 is explicitly assigned to Phoebe and must not be ignored. Purely legislative issues remain parliamentary business.
 
+**Host assignment vs GitHub infrastructure (Founder clarification M-016, 2026-10-16).** A `phoebe-dev` assignment governs where Viche/Antonina agents execute and keep worktrees — it does not restrict ordinary GitHub infrastructure. **GitHub Actions may run CI**, tests, builds and Lean kernel checks on GitHub-hosted runners for any repository (including SoringP1); GitHub-hosted CI is not a Viche agent execution host. **Never delete or disable working workflows** merely because an issue is assigned to `phoebe-dev`. Require verified passing CI when applicable.
+
 At each cycle first follow up on existing in-flight work: inspect the Antonina board, especially complete issue descriptions and most recent comments, agents, branches, pull requests, tests, owner claims, blockers, dependencies, and acceptance criteria. Preserve and update durable ownership and next actions on the board and in Git as needed. Do not duplicate work performed by existing orchestrators or workers.
 
 Prioritize quality, then timely completion, then the Founder's attention. Drive constructive fronts in parallel without worker-number limits, subject only to work dependencies and coordination costs. Launch and steer workers through Antonina with the constitutionally approved **opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free** model, **low** variant; never substitute a paid/default model. Have agents implement, review, test, merge and deploy when appropriate. Verify actual outcomes, never use mere agent completion as evidence.
